Note = {7th International Congress and Exhibition on Arsenic in the Environment
   (As) - Environmental Arsenic in a Changing World, Chinese Acad Sci, Inst
   Urban Environm, Beijing, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUL 01-06, 2018},
Organization = {KTH Royal Inst Technol; Univ So Queensland; KWR Watercycle Res Inst;
   Univ Newcastle; Int Soc Groundwater Sustainable Dev; Inst Urban
   Environm; China Univ Geosciences; Univ S Australia, CRC CARE; China
   Assoc Sci \& Technol, China Ctr Int Sci \& Technol Exchange; OPCW},
Abstract = {A Mg/Fe-based Layered Double Hydroxide (LDH) intercalated with chloride
   (Nano iowaite), was synthesized to evaluate its performance for arsenite
   removal from water. It has a much higher arsenite uptake capacity than
   other LDHs that are commonly used for water dearsenication. The surface
   adsorption of the solution arsenite onto the iowaite samples and the
   anion exchange of the arsenite in solution with chloride, which is
   originally in the iowaite interlayers, are the primary mechanisms for
   the uptake of arsenite by iowaite.},
