Note = {10th Conference on Decision Making in Project Management, Leipzig,
   GERMANY, MAY 19-20, 2005},
Abstract = {Due to high cost of mistakes in investment choice problems, such a
   choice should be well founded. This paper presents an overview of
   existing methods for choosing the best object and a new multi-criteria
   method called Scale of Normalised and Ordered Differences (SNOD) basing
   on Verbal Decision Analysis (VDA) approach. The possibility of criteria
   interdependence is taken into account. The method was evaluated by
   statistical modelling. The method has been applied for practical cases
   in Vilnius. Risk is an integral element of any economical work. It must
   be estimated and minimised. The method SNOD can be applied to
   determining investments risk in construction.},
