Organization = {Inner Mongolia Univ},
Abstract = {Organic agricultural development is an adaptation strategy to climate
   change, is a concrete and promising option for new countryside
   construction or urban-rural integrated development and has additional
   potential as a mitigation strategy. Mitigation and adaptation based on
   organic agricultural development can build on well-established
   traditional Chinese peasant's practice because organic agriculture is a
   sustainable livelihood strategy with thousands of years in use in China.
   The paper argues that subsidies for agricultural development may be
   justified by a mitigation or adaptation strategy. This paper therefore
   highlights some of the persistent challenges associated with sustainable
   organic agricultural development in China. We aim to explore how organic
   agricultural development can maintain sustainable rural development and
   thereby serve as mitigation and an adaptation option is a possible
   future transition towards a low-carbon economy.},
