   Human-Computer Interaction (HCII), Orlando, FL, JUL 26-31, 2019},
Abstract = {A product design elements evaluation model was proposed, which was
   constructed by eye tracking experiments, using eye movement indicators
   such as first gaze time, gaze order, and number of times of return, to
   accurately and effectively analyze product model and quantify users'
   emotion. The purpose of sorting the product model contribution was
   achieved through the weight calculation of the design elements. The
   soymilk machine shape was used as a case to verify the rationality of
   the evaluation model. The results showed that the ``cup{''} part of the
   soymilk machine was the most concerned by the subjects, while the
   ``handle{''} part was the least concerned. At the same time, the further
   research direction of design elements evaluation in eye movement
   experiment and the coupling between design elements, and product
   modeling image were discussed at the end of the article. The further
   research directions and experimental design methods were clarified.},
