Pages = {263-274},
Note = {13th International Conference of the African Association of Remote
   Sensing of the Environment-AARSE, Kigali, RWANDA, OCT 24-28, 2022},
Abstract = {Land subdivision is very important as people need to buy land for their
   Construction Projects, Agriculture activities or other projects related
   to land. Thus incorrect land subdivision can cause land conflicts for
   land owners in urban and rural areas. Therefore, if land surveying in
   not done well this might result in endless land problems. It is for this
   reason Land practitioners must take into consideration proper land
   surveying to avoid land difficulties which might come in case this is
   not done properly. In Rwanda people are doing land projects including
   Construction, buying and Selling land as well as other land related
   projects depending on their interests and this trend will keep growing
   even in the future. Thus this study assessed the impact of surveying
   instruments in land subdivision in Rwanda for proper land surveying and
   land related conflict reduction through precise land surveying.
   Furthermore, the Case of Rwanda in Buyanja village of Rwamagana
   district, as the present project has been conducted with the main
   objective of land demarcation process in Buyanja village, the study
   specific objectives collecting data of field parcels boundaries of
   Sample parcels of Buyanja village, to process and produce cadastral maps
   that show parcels boundaries of sampled parcels and to compare existing
   cadastral map and new cadastral map of sampled parcels. Land demarcation
   should be the firmly proof of ownership of the land parcel and be able
   to solve any problems regarding to it, but due to the process of Land
   demarcation in 2008 the result shown that 84\% of all parcels were only
   been recorded and others 16\% were not, due to that those whom their
   parcels were recorded they all believed that their parcels are well
   recorded. From 2009 up now land surveyor were added to those who help to
   solve boundaries problems by using their knowledge and instruments of
   high accuracy. The aim of this research was to identify the errors in
   land demarcation process and it provides cadastral map of accurate
   measurement which conduct to appropriate taxation and expropriation
   which and match with the LAIS boundaries to show the errors to achieve
   these objectives field work was conducted Buyanja village in order to
   collect primary and secondary data with regard to the scope of this
   research. During data collection DGPS which called UNISTRONG was used
   and ArcGIS was used during analysis the data collected in order to
   answer research question. The data used were collected from 13 parcels
   selected using random sampling to determine whether the result recorded
   in land titles are the same to the ones on field. These sample parcels
   are located in Munyiginya sector, Buyanja village of Rwamagana district
   Eastern province. The result shows that 13 of parcels which were
   surveyed and chosen randomly in Buyanja village, almost 85\% were
   affected by first land demarcation which rise the boundaries problems
   soon or late, and 15\% are those which is recorded and found not many
   mistakes were committed and when accurate instrument was used found that
   it is not fit with the boundaries of parcel available in land title of
   owners are recommended to follow the process of collection.},
