   AUSTRALIA, AUG 20-24, 2007},
Organization = {Hlth Informat Soc Australia},
Abstract = {Organizational knowledge management (KM) research studies the nature of
   knowledge, the scope of KM, the factors and mechanisms that affect KM
   outcomes, as well as theoretical KM frameworks. This paper discusses the
   implications of past studies for the KM efforts in the human genetic
   variation (HGV) research domain and presents a HGV-KM research model.
   This model identifies the context of HGV KM studies' the predispositions
   and factors that may impact KM outcomes, and important KM processes. It
   also represents the relationships among these issues. Applying the
   model, further studies will point the way for improved capture and
   dissemination of HGV knowledge from routine HGV research activities to
   contribute to the global genetics knowledgebase.},
