   03-08, 2001},
Organization = {Int Soc Theoret Psychol},
Abstract = {The critical psychology movement has made us aware of the political and
   ideological underpinnings and implications of psychological theory,
   methods, and research findings. One concern is that psychological theory
   and research will be discounted by others based on the perception that
   they are ``politically biased.{''} I address the possibility of moving
   beyond this new form of legitimation crisis by proposing a
   transpositional hermenuetic.},
