Note = {Conference on Urban Environmental Pollution - Overcoming Obstacles to
   Sustainability and Quality of Life, Boston, MA, JUN 20-23, 2010},
Abstract = {Traffic emissions are measured at several locations along and across a
   non-homogeneous symmetrical street canyon in Nicosia, with a single
   off-centre traffic lane. Under several background wind conditions, CO
   concentrations were higher on the pavement near the traffic lane at
   various locations and heights within the street, as opposed to predicted
   flow regimes for street canyons in these winds. The levels of pollution
   experienced at ground level, depending greatly on street geometry and
   local wind conditions, are affected by the location of the traffic
   lanes, and thus might exceed safe pollution levels for long periods in
   time. (C) 2009 Published by Elsevier BV},
