   SEP 17-19, 2021},
Abstract = {Visual, audio, and emotional perception by human beings have been an
   interesting research topic in the past few decades.
   Electroencephalography (EEG) signals are one of the ways to represent
   human brain activity. It has been shown, that different brain networks
   correspond to processes corresponding to varieties of emotional stimuli.
   In this paper, we demonstrate a deep learning architecture for the movie
   identification task from the EEG response using Convolutional Neural
   Network (CNN). The dataset includes nine movie clips that span across
   different emotional states. The EEG time series data has been collected
   for 20 participants. Given one second EEG response of particular
   participant, we tried to predict its corresponding movie ID. We have
   also discussed the various pre-processing steps for data cleaning and
   data augmentation process. All the participants have been considered in
   both train and test data. We obtained 80.22\% test accuracy for this
   movie classification task. We also tried cross participant testing using
   the same model and the performance was poor for the unseen participants.
   Our result gives insight toward the creation of identifiable patterns in
   the brain during audiovisual perception.},
