   \& Hlth; Int Council Res \& Innovat Bldg \& Construct; European Commiss
   Asia Pro Eco Programme Promot Sustainable Solut Environm Europe \& Asia;
   Korean Soc Indoor Environm; Soc Indoor Environm},
Abstract = {Concentration of VOCs in indoor air was measured in more than 300
   dwellings where residents reported symptoms. The results of 645 air
   measurements collected during 2003-04 are reported here. The dwellings
   were located in an urban area in the city of Helsinki and most of them
   were apartments. Measures were based on The Health Protection Act of
   Finland because there were suspicions of a health hazard. The main aim
   of this study was to find out which compounds commonly appear in
   dwellings where residents have symptoms. Altogether 49 volatile organic
   target compounds were selected to indicate the state of air quality. The
   study showed which target compounds in our list are of interest in
   assessing healthy conditions. Most abundant compounds were pinene,
   toluene, limonene, TXIB, hexanal and 2-ethyl-1-hexanol. Halogenated
   compounds were relatively rare in the Finnish homes of the present time.
   Incidence of some other carcinogen and genotoxic compounds, like benzene
   and styrene, was high.},
